# Ansible managed (games role)
#
# RetroArch's udev input driver reads /dev/input/event* directly, and the distro's rules
# grant the seat user an ACL on joysticks alone, so it has a gamepad, no pointer and no
# keys. Tag the rest for uaccess too.
#
# Sorts after 60-input-id.rules, which classifies each device, and before
# 73-seat-late.rules, which turns the tag into the ACL.

# A KVM presents an idle mouse that emits nothing and enumerates ahead of the real one,
# taking pointer 0. RetroArch aggregates motion across all mice, so the cursor moves
# while every click lands on the dead device. Enumeration order is not stable, so an
# index cannot fix it: drop this device's mouse classification instead. Harmless on a
# host without it, and matched by USB id rather than host name, the repo being public.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{idVendor}=="09eb", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0131", ENV{ID_INPUT_MOUSE}=="1", ENV{ID_INPUT_MOUSE}="0"

# After the rule above, so the suppressed device is skipped here too.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ENV{ID_INPUT_MOUSE}=="1", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ENV{ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD}=="1", TAG+="uaccess"
